.docname {Plugin Package Format}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

BakingRL v2 packages are described by `bakingrl.plugin.json`.

## Minimal Manifest

```json
{
  "schema": "bakingrl.plugin/2",
  "id": "com.example.my-package",
  "name": "My Package",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "compatibility": {
    "runtimeApi": "0.3.0",
    "sdk": "0.3.0"
  },
  "exports": {
    "visuals": {
      "scoreboard": {
        "entry": "dist/visuals/scoreboard.js",
        "defaultSize": [760, 128],
        "settings": "schemas/scoreboard-settings.json"
      }
    },
    "layouts": {
      "stream": {
        "path": "templates/stream-layout.json",
        "title": "Stream Layout"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Export Types

- `exports.visuals`: browser ESM modules mounted in overlays and pages.
- `exports.components`: reusable visual components loaded by visuals.
- `exports.services`: sandboxed backend modules with callable methods.
- `exports.connectors`: backend modules with explicit network permissions.
- `exports.pages`: importable page templates.
- `exports.layouts`: importable overlay layout templates.
- `exports.configuration`: private fixed-size plugin configuration page.

## Top-Level Fields

`schema`

Must be `bakingrl.plugin/2`.

`id`

Stable package identity. Use a reverse-DNS style value such as
`com.example.scoreboard`. Do not use the reserved `plugin.` runtime prefix.

`name`

Human-readable package name.

`version`

Package version. Use semantic versions so the host and future marketplace can
compare updates predictably.

`compatibility`

Runtime compatibility declaration. `runtimeApi` is required; `sdk` is optional
but recommended for diagnostics.

`exports`

Capabilities provided by the package. A package must export at least one
capability.

`imports`

Optional package references consumed by this package. Current fields are
`components` and `services`.

`permissions`

Optional host-enforced permissions for bus events, registry keys, network
hosts, and storage paths.

`settings`

Optional package-level settings schema path.

## Runtime Compatibility

`compatibility.runtimeApi` is required for packages targeting current BakingRL
hosts. The SDK scaffolder initializes it with the current runtime API version.

Current host support is `>=0.3.0 <0.4.0`. Packages outside that range can still
be installed for inspection, but the host disables them and refuses activation
until they are rebuilt for a compatible runtime API.

## Visual Instance Settings

`exports.visuals.<name>.settings` can point to a JSON Schema file. BakingRL uses
that schema to render typed instance settings in the page and layout editors,
instead of forcing users to edit raw JSON.

Settings schemas should be JSON Schema objects with `properties`. Use
`title`, `description`, `default`, `required`, numeric/string bounds, and
primitive option lists to make the generated editor form readable.

Supported field shapes in the current host UI:

- `type: "string"`, including `format: "color"`;
- `type: "number"` or `type: "integer"`;
- `type: "boolean"`;
- `enum`, `oneOf`, or `anyOf` options with primitive values;
- `type: "array"` with primitive options declared on `items`.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "title": "Scoreboard Settings",
  "properties": {
    "accent": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "color",
      "default": "#38bdf8"
    },
    "showBoost": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": true
    },
    "density": {
      "type": "string",
      "default": "comfortable",
      "oneOf": [
        { "const": "compact", "title": "Compact" },
        { "const": "comfortable", "title": "Comfortable" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

## Page Templates

`exports.pages` contains templates for host-owned page layouts. Importing a
template does not create a plugin-owned route or window. BakingRL assigns fresh
IDs and timestamps, tracks template provenance, and then lets users edit the
page like any other page.

## Layout Templates

`exports.layouts` contains templates for overlay layouts. A template is
imported into BakingRL's host-owned layout list; it does not create an overlay
runtime by itself. Users can then route the imported layout to the in-game
overlay or OBS stream output.

Layout template IDs, layer IDs, item IDs, timestamps, and template provenance
may be rewritten during import. Keep portable behavior in package/export
references and item settings rather than relying on template IDs.

## Configuration Page

`exports.configuration` declares one private page rendered only from the package
detail configuration tab. It is not listed as a user-importable page template,
and its visuals are not available in the normal visual picker.

The host forces the configuration canvas to `1200x740`, regardless of the page
file dimensions.

```json
{
  "exports": {
    "configuration": {
      "path": "pages/configuration.json",
      "title": "Package Settings",
      "visuals": {
        "settingsPanel": {
          "entry": "dist/configuration/settings-panel.js",
          "defaultSize": [1200, 740]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Configuration visuals are private to that page. Do not reference them from
normal pages, overlays, or public layout templates.

## Imports And Permissions

Imports declare package capabilities this package expects to consume:

```json
{
  "imports": {
    "components": ["com.example.ui/TeamBadge"],
    "services": ["com.example.stats/matchStats"]
  }
}
```

Permissions declare host-mediated capabilities:

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "bus": {
      "read": ["UpdateState", "GoalScored"],
      "publish": ["plugin.com.example.scoreboard.*"]
    },
    "registry": {
      "read": ["plugin.com.example.scoreboard.*"],
      "write": ["plugin.com.example.scoreboard.*"]
    },
    "network": {
      "http": ["api.example.com"],
      "websocket": ["stream.example.com"]
    },
    "storage": ["plugin://self/*"]
  }
}
```

The SDK can type these fields, but the host is the enforcement boundary.

## Distribution Bundle

The `.brlp` format is a ZIP archive. Required:

```txt
bakingrl.plugin.json
```

Supported:

```txt
dist/
assets/
schemas/
templates/
manifest.hashes.json
signature.ed25519
```

The helper CLI can generate hashes, signatures, and `.brlp` archives.

```sh
npm run pack
npm run keygen -- signing-key.json
npm run pack -- --sign signing-key.json
```

## Versioning

Use semantic versions in package manifests. BakingRL treats package IDs as
stable identities, so avoid changing an ID after publishing.
